doc.para:
@set directive The @set directive evaluates a conditional compilation expression and discards the result. The syntax is as follows:
@set(expression)
In "expression", you write a conditional compilation expression. The following operators can be used here:
, = != == || && | ^ & < > <= >= + - % * / ! + - ( )
Please see for the meanings of these operators. However, the only supported data type is integers. In addition, arbitrary variables and literal values can be used. For variable naming rules, the same rules as for variable names and literals in apply. However, variables used in the preprocessor and variables used in the TJS2 script do not interfere with each other (they do not share the same namespace).

@if directive, @endif directive
　The @if directive evaluates a conditional compilation expression, and if the result is 0, it skips interpretation of the script until the next @endif. If the result is non-zero, it is interpreted.
　The syntax is as follows:

	@if(expression)              ...         @endif

	Specify a conditional compilation expression in "expression". @if ... @endif blocks can be nested.


	@if(flag==0)  // Variables that have not been assigned anything yet are considered to be 0
		@set(flag=1)
		****
	@endif
	// ↑ Makes the compilation of the script written in the **** portion happen only once

	@if(version>=0x02040009)
		@if(flag)
			****
		@endif
	@endif 
	// ↑ Compiles the **** portion only when version is 0x02040009 (2.4.9) or higher and flag is non-zero
